From: Mohamad Raizudeen <raizudeen.kerneldev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:55:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mm: zswap: remove dead length check in zswap_store_page()

zswap_compress() never succeeds with entry->length == 0, so the condition
is always true.  Remove it.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261123032512.6119-1-raizudeen.kerneldev@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Mohamad Raizudeen <raizudeen.kerneldev@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reviewed-by: Joshua Hahn <joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Yosry Ahmed <yosry@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Nhat Pham <nphamcs@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Cc: Chengming Zhou <chengming.zhou@linux.dev>
Cc: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>

 mm/zswap.c |    6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
---
 mm/zswap.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/zswap.c b/mm/zswap.c
index a2e0314db1cf0..6a66b898ab470 100644
--- a/mm/zswap.c
+++ b/mm/zswap.c
@@ -1597,10 +1597,8 @@ static bool zswap_store_page(struct folio *folio, long index,
 	entry->swpentry = page_swpentry;
 	entry->objcg = objcg;
 	entry->referenced = true;
-	if (entry->length) {
-		INIT_LIST_HEAD(&entry->lru);
-		zswap_lru_add(entry);
-	}
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&entry->lru);
+	zswap_lru_add(entry);
 
 	return true;
 
-- 
